Tournament Analysis over proof abstractions
rank | route | outscore | note
--- | --- | --- | ---
1 | explicit layer word | 5 | finite symbolic certificate; no search
2 | traceable section | 4 | unit spine is retained as a section over the carrier quotient
3 | ear/slab gluing | 3 | local traceable blocks glue when endpoints are unit-adjacent
4 | frontier-gain search | 2 | finds the slab but does not itself prove the template
5 | point-order tournament | 1 | diagnostic only; can forget the section
score histogram: {1:1,2:1,3:1,4:1,5:1}
directed 3-cycles: 0
Hamiltonian path count: 1

Abstract reading: a unit spine is a traceable section.  The layer word
is a Gray code on an 8-vertex slab, and the bridge vector is the gluing
map between consecutive fibers.  The tournament tie path should remember
that section; otherwise the point-order quotient can create a fake flop.
